{"title":"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfies the equation\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/0/cd0819b6a5a64ae184b0eec5b9edd6b9afb6942d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25^{-2} = \\frac{5^{48/x}}{5^{26/x} \\cdot 25^{17/x}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"165\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/9/df939ae28c8122b88e1f117bf649c5787dead00e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 2 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 3 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 5 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 6 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"353\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Manipulate the powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in order to get a clean expression.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/7/ee7b66e25c28807e2bfea090fc8f89c5d6b41aa2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{5^{\\frac{48}{x}}}{5^{\\frac{26}{x}} \\cdot 25^{\\frac{17}{x}}} = \\frac{5^{\\frac{48}{x}}}{5^{\\frac{26}{x}} \\cdot 5^{\\frac{34}{x}}} = 5^{\\frac{48}{x}-(\\frac{26}{x}+\\frac{34}{x})} = 5^{-\\frac{12}{x}}\\]\" width=\"334\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/d/5cdb1a2ed954ee8fda8aae01c8a9032b16e28bba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[25^{-2} = (5^2)^{-2} = 5^{-4}\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/9/219e5f75112057ae2f3f02acf33d2ea76bc8581b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5^{-4} = 5^{-\\frac{12}{x}}\\]\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>If two numbers are equal, and their bases are equal, then their exponents are equal as well.  Set the two exponents equal to each other.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/9/d09c287805fe3b593991cb2a5e5cbd20b040094e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}-4&amp;=\\frac{-12}{x}\\\\ -4x&amp;=-12\\\\ x&amp;=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) \\ } 3}\\end{align*}\" width=\"118\" height=\"98\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B\">2003 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<